{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GBknenfyPF5e7x4GRQfBg9","type":"tool_result","content":"### 2.9 Test runner pipeline\n\n1. `test/index.ts` imports every test module (`test/<area>/*.ts`); it is\n   the only test entry. Tests use `@substrate-system/tapzero` (`test`,\n   `t.ok`, `t.equal`, `t.deepEqual`, async tests).\n2. `npm run build:test` runs `scripts/bundle.ts --test`: the 2.5 options\n   with `entryPoints: ['test/index.ts']`, `outfile: 'test/test-bundle.js'`,\n   `tsconfig: 'tsconfig.json'`, no shebang line in the banner (the\n   `require` shim stays), no defines, no metafile.\n3. `npm run test:tap` runs `node test/test-bundle.js` piped to `tap-spec`\n   under `bash -o pipefail`, so the script fails when the bundle exits\n   non-zero (a failed assertion, an uncaught error, a crash before the\n   plan) even if the formatter exits 0. Bash is available on both\n   supported platforms.\n4. `npm test` builds the real bundle first, because the bundle smoke tests\n   (5.1) spawn `dist/cli.js`.\n5. Tests find the repo root from the bundle location:\n   `new URL('..', import.meta.url)` (the bundle lives in `test/`).\n6. Opt-in live provider tests (`ROAST_LIVE_*`) live under `test/live/`\n   with their own entry `test/live/index.ts`, bundled to\n   `test/live-bundle.js` by `scripts/bundle.ts --live` and run by\n   `npm run test:live`. `test/index.ts` never imports them, so `npm test`\n   cannot reach the network even with the variables set. CI never runs\n   `test:live`.\n7. Test hygiene that the tooling assumes: tests create temporary Git\n   repositories with `GIT_AUTHOR_*`/`GIT_COMMITTER_*` set in the child\n   environment (CI runners have no Git identity), isolate `HOME` and\n   `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`, and compare directories after `realpath` (macOS\n   temp dirs are `/var/...` while Git prints `/private/var/...`).\n\nThe Go-specific notes go away: there is no race detector, so CI sets no\n`GOFLAGS`; the rule that a `go` subprocess under `-race` must not set\n`CGO_ENABLED=0` has no TS successor; `go mod tidy`, `gofmt`, `go vet`, and\nstaticcheck U1000 are replaced by `tsc` (unused locals surface through the\n`@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars` lint rule). The only Go build left\nafter M0 is the differential harness's baseline binary (2.13), which it\nbuilds with `GOFLAGS` removed from the environment.\n\n### 2.10 Package check (`scripts/check-pack.ts`, slimmed)\n\nRun as `npm run check:pack` after `npm run build`, in CI and in\n`prepublishOnly`. Operates on `process.cwd()` so tests can run it in a\nfixture. Steps:\n\n1. `npm pack --dry-run --json` in the package root (no `--workspaces`).\n   Non-zero exit: print npm's stderr, fail.\n2. Parse stdout: npm 12 prints an object keyed by package name, older npm\n   an array; accept both and take the single result's `files[].path`.\n3. Fail unless the tarball lists each of `dist/cli.js`,\n   `dist/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt`, `roast.schema.json`, `LICENSE.txt`,\n   `LICENSE-MIT.txt`, `LICENSE-APACHE.txt`.\n4. Fail when `package.json` declares no `license`, or declares a non-empty\n   `dependencies` or any `optionalDependencies`.\n5. Fail when `dist/cli.js` on disk does not start with\n   `#!/usr/bin/env node\\n` or is not executable by its owner.\n6. On failure print every problem (one per line, prefixed by\n   `packaging check failed:`), then the hint to run `npm run build` and\n   check `files`, and exit 1. On success print one summary line, exit 0.\n\n### 2.11 Release lifecycle\n\nPublishing is local only (no CI publish job), as at the baseline. The\ntemplate's npm lifecycle replaces `scripts/release.ts`, `version.ts`,\n`check-release.ts`, `platforms.ts`, and `licenses.sh`:\n\n```\nnpm version <major|minor|patch|x.y.z>\n  preversion      npm run lint\n  (npm writes the version into package.json)\n  version         README toc, CHANGELOG.md via auto-changelog, git add\n// The single test entry: imports every test module.\nimport './tooling/buildinfo.js'\nimport './tooling/startup.js'\nimport './tooling/bundle.js'\nimport './tooling/run-import.js'\nimport './tooling/assets.js'\nimport './tooling/test-tap.js'\nimport './tooling/licenses.js'\nimport './tooling/check-package.js'\nimport './textsafe/textsafe.js'\nimport './gocompat/strings.js'\nimport './gocompat/duration.js'\nimport './gocompat/match.js'\nimport './fsutil/atomic.js'\nimport './git/git.js'\nimport './util/pool.js'\nimport { spawn } from 'node:child_process'\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url'\n\n// The test bundle lives in test/, so the repository root is one up.\nexport const ROOT = fileURLToPath(new URL('..', import.meta.url))\n\nexport interface SpawnResult {\n    code:number|null;\n    stdout:string;\n    stderr:string;\n}\n\n// Runs a command to completion and collects its output.\nexport function run (\n    command:string,\n    args:string[],\n    opts:{ cwd?:string, env?:NodeJS.ProcessEnv } = {}\n):Promise<SpawnResult> {\n    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n        const child = spawn(command, args, {\n            cwd:opts.cwd ?? ROOT,\n            env:opts.env ?? process.env,\n            stdio:['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe'],\n        })\n        let stdout = ''\n        let stderr = ''\n        child.stdout.setEncoding('utf8')\n        child.stderr.setEncoding('utf8')\n        child.stdout.on('data', chunk => { stdout += chunk })\n        child.stderr.on('data', chunk => { stderr += chunk })\n        child.on('error', reject)\n        child.on('close', code => resolve({ code, stdout, stderr }))\n    })\n}\n// The one git runner. Every area runs git through here; scope and context\n// add their specialized wrappers (patch capping, streaming) on top.\n\nimport { spawn } from 'node:child_process'\n\nexport class GitError extends Error {\n    exitCode:number|null\n    stderr:string\n\n    constructor (exitCode:number|null, signal:string|null, stderr:string) {\n        const status = exitCode === null ?\n            `signal: ${signal}` :\n            `exit status ${exitCode}`\n        const detail = stderr.trim()\n        super(detail ? `${status}: ${detail}` : status)\n        this.name = 'GitError'\n        this.exitCode = exitCode\n        this.stderr = stderr\n    }\n}\n\nexport interface GitRunOpts {\n    // Kills the child on abort; the call rejects with the signal's reason.\n    signal?:AbortSignal;\n    // The environment git runs with, normally the CLI context's env. Only\n    // when absent is process.env used.\n    env?:NodeJS.ProcessEnv;\n    // Variables merged over `env`.\n    extraEnv?:Record<string, string>;\n    // Written to stdin, which is then closed.\n    input?:Buffer|string;\n}\n\n// How long a child gets after SIGTERM before SIGKILL.\nconst KILL_GRACE_MS = 1000\n\ninterface Exit {\n    code:number|null;\n    signal:string|null;\n    stdout:Buffer;\n    stderr:Buffer;\n}\n\nfunction runGit (\n    repo:string,\n    args:readonly string[],\n    opts:GitRunOpts\n):Promise<Exit> {\n    const { signal } = opts\n    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n        if (signal?.aborted) {\n            reject(signal.reason)\n            return\n        }\n        const env = { ...(opts.env ?? process.env), ...opts.extraEnv }\n        const child = spawn('git', ['-C', repo, ...args], {\n            env,\n            stdio:['pipe', 'pipe', 'pipe'],\n        })\n        const out:Buffer[] = []\n        const err:Buffer[] = []\n        let killTimer:NodeJS.Timeout|undefined\n        let spawnError:Error|undefined\n\n        function onAbort ():void {\n            child.kill('SIGTERM')\n            killTimer = setTimeout(() => child.kill('SIGKILL'),\n                KILL_GRACE_MS)\n        }\n        signal?.addEventListener('abort', onAbort, { once:true })\n\n        child.stdout.on('data', (chunk:Buffer) => out.push(chunk))\n        child.stderr.on('data', (chunk:Buffer) => err.push(chunk))\n        child.on('error', e => { spawnError ??= e })\n        // A child that exits without reading stdin closes the pipe; that\n        // EPIPE is not a git failure.\n        child.stdin.on('error', () => {})\n        if (opts.input !== undefined) child.stdin.end(opts.input)\n        else child.stdin.end()\n\nsrc/git/git.ts:6:export class GitError extends Error {\nsrc/git/git.ts:22:export interface GitRunOpts {\nsrc/git/git.ts:102:export async function git (\nsrc/git/git.ts:116:export async function gitOk (\nsrc/git/git.ts:126:export async function gitRoot (\nsrc/buildinfo.ts:5:export interface BuildInfo {\nsrc/buildinfo.ts:11:export const buildInfo:BuildInfo = {\nsrc/buildinfo.ts:24:export function formatBuildInfo (info:BuildInfo):string {\nsrc/textsafe/textsafe.ts:116:export function text (s:string):string {\nsrc/textsafe/textsafe.ts:122:export function line (s:string):string {\nsrc/textsafe/textsafe.ts:128:export function textBytes (b:Uint8Array):string {\nsrc/textsafe/textsafe.ts:133:export function lineBytes (b:Uint8Array):string {\nimport { test } from '@substrate-system/tapzero'\nimport {\n    text,\n    line,\n    textBytes,\n    lineBytes,\n} from '../../src/textsafe/textsafe.js'\n\n// Go vectors from internal/textsafe/textsafe_test.go (TestTextEscapesControls)\n// whose input is valid UTF-8, so a JS string can carry them.\nconst TEXT_VECTORS:[string, string][] = [\n    ['plain text', 'plain text'],\n    ['keeps\\nnewline\\tand tab', 'keeps\\nnewline\\tand tab'],\n    ['esc\\x1b[2J', 'esc\\\\x1b[2J'],\n    ['osc\\x1b]0;title\\x07', 'osc\\\\x1b]0;title\\\\x07'],\n    ['nul\\x00 del\\x7f', 'nul\\\\x00 del\\\\x7f'],\n    ['lone\\rcarriage return', 'lone\\\\x0dcarriage return'],\n    ['crlf\\r\\nline', 'crlf\\nline'],\n    ['c1 csi\\u009b2J', 'c1 csi\\\\u009b2J'],\n    ['c1 nel\\u0085', 'c1 nel\\\\u0085'],\n    ['unicode \\u00e9 \\u2713 stays', 'unicode \\u00e9 \\u2713 stays'],\n]\n\ntest('text escapes controls and keeps newlines, tabs, non-ASCII', t => {\n    for (const [input, want] of TEXT_VECTORS) {\n        t.equal(text(input), want, JSON.stringify(input))\n        t.equal(textBytes(Buffer.from(input)), want,\n            'bytes ' + JSON.stringify(input))\n    }\n})","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4755d765-a6df-4b24-a4bc-26dbeaee612d","uuid":"863d3936-fb91-4755-b534-32936d034e18","timestamp":"2026-11-18T19:23:59.924Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"### 2.9 Test runner pipeline\n\n1. `test/index.ts` imports every test module (`test/<area>/*.ts`); it is\n   the only test entry. Tests use `@substrate-system/tapzero` (`test`,\n   `t.ok`, `t.equal`, `t.deepEqual`, async tests).\n2. `npm run build:test` runs `scripts/bundle.ts --test`: the 2.5 options\n   with `entryPoints: ['test/index.ts']`, `outfile: 'test/test-bundle.js'`,\n   `tsconfig: 'tsconfig.json'`, no shebang line in the banner (the\n   `require` shim stays), no defines, no metafile.\n3. `npm run test:tap` runs `node test/test-bundle.js` piped to `tap-spec`\n   under `bash -o pipefail`, so the script fails when the bundle exits\n   non-zero (a failed assertion, an uncaught error, a crash before the\n   plan) even if the formatter exits 0. Bash is available on both\n   supported platforms.\n4. `npm test` builds the real bundle first, because the bundle smoke tests\n   (5.1) spawn `dist/cli.js`.\n5. Tests find the repo root from the bundle location:\n   `new URL('..', import.meta.url)` (the bundle lives in `test/`).\n6. Opt-in live provider tests (`ROAST_LIVE_*`) live under `test/live/`\n   with their own entry `test/live/index.ts`, bundled to\n   `test/live-bundle.js` by `scripts/bundle.ts --live` and run by\n   `npm run test:live`. `test/index.ts` never imports them, so `npm test`\n   cannot reach the network even with the variables set. CI never runs\n   `test:live`.\n7. Test hygiene that the tooling assumes: tests create temporary Git\n   repositories with `GIT_AUTHOR_*`/`GIT_COMMITTER_*` set in the child\n   environment (CI runners have no Git identity), isolate `HOME` and\n   `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`, and compare directorie