{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChAx9NYWzdzkiQsJJ33pt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] `ExitCode` constants are 0 to 5 as in 01 / 2.2, and `exitCode` maps wrapped cancellation, auth, and usage errors (through `cause`) to 5, 3, 2, and anything else to 4.\n[x] `errorCategoryFor` returns `none`, `findings`, `usage`, `auth`, `endpoint`, `resource_limit` (budget, deadline, no final call), `cancelled`, and `partial` for the matching wrapped errors and codes.\n[x] `writeError` in text form escapes control bytes (an ESC in the message never reaches stderr); in JSON form stderr parses as an object with `error_category`, `message`, `exit_code`, and a message containing `<>&` round-trips unchanged.\n[x] `--error-format yaml` exits 2 with a text error; a parse failure with `--error-format json` given yields a JSON error on stderr.\n[x] Unknown commands and flags exit 2: `bogus`, `config bogus`, `completion`, `eval`, `install`, `replay`, a root positional, and an unknown flag.\n[x] `--help` exits 0 with help on stdout and needs no config, Git repository, or network.\n[x] `--version` exits 0 and prints the build string on stdout; on a subcommand registered for the test it is an unknown flag (exit 2).\n[x] Bare `roast` outside a Git repository exits 0 with help on stdout; explicit `review` outside a Git repository exits 2.\n[x] A command registered through the registration API that throws a wrapped `CancelledError` while `io.signal` is aborted exits 5 with category `cancelled`; one that throws `ExitSignal(1)` exits 1 and writes nothing to stderr.\n[x] The entry signal handler aborts on the first signal and calls the injected exit with 130 on the second; the EPIPE handler exits with the computed code and writes no stack trace.\n[x] `promptYesDefault` returns true for empty, `y`, `Y`, `yes`, false for anything else, and false on EOF with no input.\n[x] `readSecret` on a fake TTY stream treats `\\x03` as cancellation (exit 5 when it reaches `run`); on a non-TTY stream several answers fed as one string `\"a\\nb\\n\"` are read by consecutive calls sharing one `LineReader`.\n[x] The default `interactiveTerminals` returns false for non-file streams such as test buffers.\n[x] `cleanEnv` removes `ANTHROPIC_*`, `OPENAI_*`, `OPENROUTER_*`, `ROAST_*` (any case) and keeps other variables.\n[x] `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run test:ts` pass; `go test ./...` still passes.\n\nTicket 04 is done. All 15 checklist items have passing tests, and the work is in six commits. `npm run lint`, `typecheck` and `test:ts` (596 assertions) pass, and so does the full `npm test`, which includes `go test ./...`. The notes file `.redeye/notes.md` is not committed.\n\n**What later tickets plug into:**\n- **Adding a command:** each command is a `CommandDef` (`src/cli/command.ts`), and an area adds its command to the list in `src/cli/commands.ts`. Tests add their own with `registerCommand`, which returns a function that removes it. A handler gets a context with cwd, env, signal, `fetch` and one shared `LineReader`. It throws `UsageError`, `ExitSignal` or any other error, and `run` turns that into the exit code and the stderr output.\n- **When handlers run:** the yargs handlers only record which command was picked. `run` calls the real handler after parsing succeeds, so a parse error can't be confused with an error from the command. Leftover positional arguments (including anything after `--`) are rejected in that same step.\n- **Review placeholder:** `src/cli/review.ts` holds the default command. It only handles bare `roast` outside a repository; everything else is a usage error until ticket 20 replaces it.\n- **Entry handlers:** the signal and EPIPE handlers live in `src/cli/process.ts` with an injectable `exit`, and `src/cli.ts` wires them up. An end-to-end test spawns `dist/cli.js` with stdout already closed and checks that it exits 0 with an empty stderr. Before the fix it crashed with an unhandled EPIPE and exited 1.\n\n**Where I departed from the ticket:**\n- **No debug tracing.** AGENTS.md says no `src/` module may import `@substrate-system/debug` until it passes the license check, so the `roast:cli` namespace isn't wired up yet.\n- **Test cleanup wrapper.** tapzero has no end-of-test hook, so I added a `test` wrapper in `test/helpers/test.ts` that gives Go-style `t.cleanup`. `simulateTerminals(t, value)` and `captureBrowser(t)` register their restore through it.\n- **Root help has no Commands section yet.** yargs leaves it out while the default command is the only one registered; it will appear once another area registers a command.\n\nI added the CLI-core conventions to AGENTS.md."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1398,"cache_read_input_tokens":149895,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1398},"output_tokens":788,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4755d765-a6df-4b24-a4bc-26dbeaee612d","uuid":"fbf8dfa5-91b5-4706-a606-8ede978fc60b","timestamp":"2026-11-18T19:33:03.946Z","request_id":"req_011ChAx9NHdtbfZVHhkgNHTU"}
